# =====================================================================
# TRUMPF Cutting Assistant — Chatbot provider keys
# =====================================================================
# The chatbot tries providers in this order:
#   1) Gemini    (Google AI Studio — recommended, free)
#   2) Groq      (Llama 3.3 70B — fast, free, OpenAI-compatible)
#   3) OpenRouter (free fallback models)
#   4) Offline rule-based answerer (always works, no key needed)
#
# Set as MANY keys as you want — leave the rest blank.
# If you set none, the chatbot still works (offline / demo mode).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1-MINUTE GEMINI KEY (recommended):
#   1. Open  https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
#   2. Sign in with any Google account
#   3. Click "Create API key" → "Create API key in new project"
#   4. Copy the key, paste it after GEMINI_API_KEY= below
#   5. Save this file as `.env`, then restart  `npm run dev`
#
# 1-MINUTE GROQ KEY (alternative):
#   1. Open  https://console.groq.com/keys
#   2. Sign in with Google / GitHub
#   3. Click "Create API Key", give it any name
#   4. Copy the key (starts with `gsk_`), paste after GROQ_API_KEY=
# =====================================================================

GEMINI_API_KEY=
GROQ_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
